  "notes": [
    "Ramp/cliff info comes from t3Terrain.xml rampList.",
    "Object positions come from the Objects XML (ObjectPoint / ObjectUnit).",
    "Resource clusters are single-linkage groupings at radius 6.0 map cells; a group of at most 3 base-material patches within 8.0 cells of a larger group is attached to it.",
    "resource_clusters are BASES; mineral_walls are groups of wall material - patches below 500 minerals at map start, e.g. MineralField450. Classification is per patch from its minerals at map start, never updated as patches are mined out (ruling 2026-09-24).",
    "minerals_at_start / patch_min_minerals: nominal-by-type-name; unverified against game data (2026-09-24)",
    "start_locations are the map's StartLoc candidates, not the spawns: a map may carry more than the game has players (Old Sun Temple LE: four on a map played 1v1). Spawns come from the replay - tools/spawns_from_replay.py."
